  "overview": {
    "title": "The water that defines the town",
    "p1": "Dakhla Lagoon stretches for roughly forty kilometres of shallow turquoise water, sheltered from the open Atlantic by a long sandy peninsula.",
    "p2": "This is where most visitors spend their days: kite and wing sessions on flat water, quiet walks on the shore, and sunsets that turn the lagoon gold and pink.",
    "p3": "Treat it as a landscape as much as a playground — conditions and access points vary along its length."
  },
